# fix symmetry example: 6 LJ atoms with two mirror planes (space group Pmm2)
#
# The group has 4 operators: identity, two-fold axis along z, and the
# mirror planes perpendicular to x and y.  Atoms 3 to 6 are on general
# positions and related by all 4 operators.  Atoms 1 and 2 are on the
# mirror plane y = 0, so each is its own image under the y mirror and
# they are images of each other under the x mirror and the two-fold
# axis: an orbit of 2 atoms for 4 operators.  Atoms 1 and 2 stay on the
# plane y = 0 and move as mirror images in x.

